    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "D\nener",
      "1939\nTHE LARGEST AND LAST OF PAA'S FLYING BOATS WAS THE BOEING 314. THIS\nCLIPPER INAUGURATED THE FIRST TRANSATLANTIC SERVICE IN 1939. THE PLANE\nCARRIED 56 PASSENGERS BY DAY AND 24 BY NIGHT FIRST CLASS. LENGTH WAS\n106-FEET WITH A WINGSPREAD OF 152-FEET. THE 314 CLIPPER HAD A RANGE OF\n2,000 MILES POWERED BY FOUR 1600-HORSEPOWER WRIGHT CYCLONE ENGINES WITH\nA CRUISING SPEED OF 184-MILES-PER-HOUR. THE 314 WAS ALSO THE MOST\nLUXURIOUS PLANE PAA EVER OPERATED. IT HAD SIX PASSENGER COMPARTMENTS,\nLOUNGE, AND BRIDAL SUITE.\nA TOTAL OF 12 B-314s WERE BUILT."
    ],
